    "How to use this playbook\nThis playbook explores a central idea: much of what people think, want, and do is shaped by beliefs and habits they absorbed before they learned to examine them. Family, language, education, media, social networks, work, and culture all influence how a person interprets the world. These influences are not automatically harmful, but they can become limiting when they are accepted without reflection.",
