        "The solution is not to reject every group. It is to separate belonging from intellectual surrender.",
        "You can respect your family while choosing a different career. You can value education while questioning a particular curriculum. You can work for an employer while recognising that the employer's incentives are not identical to your own.\n2.4 A practical test: identify the source of the rule\nWhen you encounter a rule about how life should work, ask:\n- Who benefits if I follow this rule?\n- What problem was this rule originally designed to solve?\n- Does that problem still exist?\n- What evidence supports the rule?\n- What are the costs of following it?\n- What are the costs of rejecting it?\n- Are there alternatives between total compliance and total rejection?\nThis method is more useful than automatically accepting or rejecting authority."
